<title>USA: EIS expects Q3 charge on Pulse purchase.</title>
<headline>EIS expects Q3 charge on Pulse purchase.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>EIS International Inc said on Tuesday it expected to take a one-time charge in the third quarter of about $1.3 million related to its acquisition of the professional services business of Pulse Technologies Inc.</p>
<p>The terms of the acquisition were not disclosed. Pulse, based in Chantilly, Va.,  offers management consulting and support for the call centers.</p>
<p>&quot;As companies continue to push the limits of technology within this industry, Pulse Technologies will help them address the growing and complex challenges they face,&quot; said Joseph Porfeli, EIS chairman and chief executive.</p>
</text>
